scratch file, do not review
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

sched
  - LIFO preempt -> priority queue keyed on (arrival, tokens_done)   GROK-4417
  - swap-out to host mem instead of drop+recompute. measured 3x on the
    long-context replay trace, need to redo with fp8 kv
  - watermark is a magic number, should be f(block_size, avg_seq)

kv
  - prefix cache eviction O(n) blocks. LRU over hashes is fine for now
  - refcount underflow if a seq is freed twice. added an assert, root cause?
  - fp8 accuracy GROK-3980 -- talked to arch, they think it's the router
    logits not the kv at all. reproduce on mini first (no router!!) to rule out

spec decode
  - bonus token double counted in accept rate. results.md is ~3% optimistic
  - draft model kv cache is separate, should share the allocator
  - tree attention never landed, branch is 6 weeks stale

tools
  - sandbox is posix-only, windows degrades to a thread. GROK-4502
    honestly should just refuse to run on windows rather than pretend
  - per-tool timeout doesn't interrupt blocking syscalls, only checks between
  - registry allows duplicate names, last one wins, silently. bad

serve
  - no backpressure on SSE writes, slow client can pin a slot
  - rate limiter is per-process. fine until we run >1 replica, which is now
  - logprobs field is accepted and ignored, someone will notice eventually

pets (GROK-4590) -- 0.5.0 candidate, currently flagged off
  - PERSISTENCE. GROK-4611. state dies with the process, which makes the whole
    thing pointless. store decision is the actual blocker, rest is polish
  - households: pets don't perceive each other. first thing every tester tried.
    shared conversation (real, expensive) vs relationship model (cheap, fake)?
    nobody has decided and I don't want to decide it alone
  - safety hasn't looked at the personas. garfield is deliberately rude and the
    refusal path inherits his register. a sarcastic refusal to something
    actually serious is a bad look. needs a register override on refusal
  - decay rates tuned by hand in one afternoon against nothing. feel right at
    ~10min sessions, almost certainly wrong at day scale. nobody has run one
    for a week
  - bird (Pascal) cut from scope, profile still in the file, gated out of
    SPECIES. delete or finish before release, don't ship it half-in
  - does the pet know it's a bot? currently unspecified so it varies by
    checkpoint, which is the worst possible answer
  - odie/garfield defaults: telemetry says ~nobody renames. worth the polish

presets
  - memory_strategy is on BotPreset but Agent doesn't take it yet, so `eval`'s
    truncate setting is silently ignored. either wire it or drop the field
  - no per-preset stop sequences beyond the defaults. fine for now
  - serving can't select a preset over HTTP. product wants it, needs a protocol
    field that isn't in the openai shape -- extension field? separate endpoint?

misc
  - drop experimental/ before any external release !!!  (pets lives there now,
    so this needs an actual decision rather than a delete)
  - telemetry/tracing.py still emits to the internal collector by default
  - vocab file is not vendored, loader errors are unhelpful when it's missing
